      "summary": ": Wednesday, 2 September: Treble Cone is open with spring conditions and fresh corduroy across the resort after overnight grooming. The mountain is currently around 3°C with winds around 43 km/h and gusts to 80 km/h, so teams are keeping a close eye on the wind as the day develops. There has been no new snow in the last 24 hours, with 82 cm recorded over the past seven days. Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and Beginner Platter are open. Home Basin and Saddle Basin are open, along with Powder Bowl, Matukituki Basin, Summit Slopes, Backcountry Access and Skinning Access. Motatapu Chutes remain closed. The resort is operating 7 of 8 terrain areas. The road is chain-free, although it is narrow in places and visitors are asked to drive slowly and give way to buses. An active road hazard remains on the access road. Guests should also take care around Lower Triple Treat, where the patrol team is enforcing the slow zone.",
